	Place this page and the following two pages after page 2-844:


	|	?WSCNTL                            Working Set Control
	|
	|	?WSCNTL [packet address]
	|	error return
	|	normal return
	|
	|
	|	Input
	|
	|	    AC0  -1 Required
	|           AC1  Reserved (Set to 0)
	|	    AC2  Address of the ?WSCNTL packet
	|
	|	Error Codes in AC0
	|
	|	ERWSM     Caller not privileged to change Working Set
	|	ERPRH     Process not in hierarchy
	|	ERMPR     System Call Parameter Address Error (Error on
	|	          accessing packet)
	|	ERRVN     Reserved field non-zero
	|	ERPVS     Packet Version not supported
	|	ERWSS     Working Set Size error (Min greater than max.
	|	          Min greater than system max, etc.)
	|	ERWST     Minimum value is greater than swapfile size.
	|	ERAWM     Caller has wired maximum already.
	|
	|
	|	Why Use It?
	|
	|	Use this system call to view or adjust the maximum and/or
	|	minimum values for the current processes working set.  Used
	|	sensibly, this can prevent a given process from using an
	|	undue share of system resources.
	|
	|
	|	Who Can Use It?
	|
	|	Any process can issue this call against itself, it cannot be
	|	issued against a target process.  Change Working Set Privilege
	|	(?PVWM) is required to increase either the working set maximum
	|	or the working set minimum.  It is not required to decrease
	|	either limit.  Note however, that once a limit is lowered,
	|	?PVWM would be needed to even put the limit back to where it
	|	was.


	AOS/VS, AOS/VS II, and AOS/RT32 System Call Dictionary, ?R Through ?Z
	Documentation Changes, Revision 1			    2-Sep-93


	|	What It Does
	|
	|	This system call will display or modify the working set
	|	minimum and maximum values stored by the system for the
	|	calling process.  If the new maximum value is smaller than
	|	the current working set size, the system will remove pages
	|	from the working set until it conforms to the new limit.
	|	In all other cases, it will merely modify the limit saved
	|	for this process.  The new limits will be used for any
	|	subsequent decisions made by memory management for the process.
	|
	|
	|	Restrictions
	|
	|	The WS minimum cannot be set larger than the swapfile size,
	|	otherwise an attempt to swap the process would fail.  The
	|	WS maximum cannot be set smaller than the current number of
	|	?WIREd pages, or smaller than the WS minimum, otherwise paging
	|	down to the new maximum would fail.  (This call cannot be used
	|	to increase the WS minimum or maximum beyond current settings
	|	without the Change Working Set Size privilege.  Reducing the
	|	minimum or maximum can be accomplished without this privilege
	|	but once the new settings are in effect, the user would be
	|	prevented from raising them back to previous levels.)
	|
	|
	|	The format of the ?WSCNTL packet and subpacket are as follows:
	|
	|
	|	                    0              15 16            31
	|			    +----------------+----------------+
	|	?WSCNTL_PKT.PKTID   | Packet identifier               |
	|                           |                                 |
	|	                    |----------------+----------------+
	|       ?WSCNTL_PKT.FUNC    | Function Code  | Reserved       |
	|       ?WSCNTL_PKT.RSVD    |                |                |
	|                           |                | (Set to zero)  |
	|                           +----------------+----------------+
	|       ?WSCNTL_PKT.SUBPKT  | Pointer to Function subpacket   |
	|                           |                                 |
	|                           +---------------------------------+
	|                           ?WSCNTL_PKT_LEN = packet length


	AOS/VS, AOS/VS II, and AOS/RT32 System Call Dictionary, ?R Through ?Z
	Documentation Changes, Revision 1			    2-Sep-93


	|	The format of the subpacket is as follows:
	|
	|
	|	                         0             15 16             31
	|	                         +----------------+----------------+
	|	?WSCNTL_MM_PKT.PKTID     | Sub-packet identifier           |
	|	                         |                                 |
	|	                         |----------------+----------------+
	|	?WSCNTL_MM_PKT.MIN       | Working Set Minimum             |
	|	                         |                |                |
	|	                         +----------------+----------------+
	|	?WSCNTL_MM_PKT.MAX       | Working Set Maximum             |
	|	                         |                                 |
	|	                         +---------------------------------+
	|	                         ?WSCNTL_MM_PKT_LEN = packet length
	|
	|
	|	The contents of the ?WSCNTL packet are as follows:
	|
	|
	|	     OFFSET              CONTENTS
	|
	|	?WSCNTLßPKT.PKTID        Set to ?WSCNTLßPKTID.
	|	?WSCNTLßPKT.FUNC         Function Code.  ?WSCNTLßGETßLIMITS to
	|	                         get the current Working Set Limits.
	|	                         ?WSCNTL_SET_LIMITS to set new Working
	|	                         Set Limits.
	|	?WSCNTLßPKT.RSVD         Reserved.  (Set to 0.)
	|	?WSCNTLßPKT.SUBPKT       Word Pointer to ?WSCNTL Subpacket.
	|
	|
	|	The contents of the ?WSCNTL subpacket are as follows:
	|
	|	     OFFSET              CONTENTS
	|
	|	?WSCNTLßMMßPKT.PKTID     Set to ?WSCNTLßMMßPKTID.
	|	?WSCNTLßMMßPKT.MIN       If function is ?WSCNTLßGETßLIMITS then
	|	                         the current Working Set minimum will
	|	                         be returned here. If the function is
	|	                         ?WSCNTLßSETßLIMITS then this will
	|	                         contain the new working set minimum.
	|	                         0 will mean no minimum value. -1 will
	|	                         mean use the system default (0.)
	|
	|	?WSCNTLßMMßPKT.MAX       If function is ?WSCNTLßGETßLIMITS then
	|	                         the current Working Set maximum will
	|	                         be returned here. If the function is
	|	                         ?WSCNTLßSETßLIMITS then this will
	|	                         contain the new working set maximum.
	|	                         -1 will mean no maximum value.


